@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — skip and delete unsubscribed addresses
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
box "Backend — Christian Fitness Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  participant "PublishingClock" as clock
end box
box "Backend — Christian Fitness Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "PurgeNewsletterSubscriptionsHandler" as h
  participant "SendDueIssueHandler" as send
end box
box "Backend — Christian Fitness Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Christian Fitness database" as db
end box
== Every issue ==
send -> db : Recipients: Status = Subscribed and the kind switched on only
db --> send : No unsubscribed address (L2-058 AC6)
== Every 30-second tick, after the due stories ==
clock -> db : Take lease on TimeProvider tick
clock -> h : Send PurgeNewsletterSubscriptionsCommand
h -> db : Pending with RequestedAt at least 30 days ago, or Unsubscribed with UnsubscribedAt at least 29 days ago (indexed by status and time)
h -> db : Delete them with their confirmations and unsubscribe tokens (L2-058 AC6, AC9)
db --> h : Count deleted
h --> clock : Count; the log carries the count only
note over h : An address that subscribed again is Pending or Subscribed and is not deleted (L2-058 AC6)
@enduml
